---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Navbar from '../components/Navbar.astro';
import RelocateCta from '../components/RelocateCta.astro';

const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'AboutPage',
  name: 'About Bellie Acres Wine',
  url: 'https://bellieacreswine.com/about/',
  description:
    'About Bellie Acres Wine — independent Temecula Valley wine-country publisher: guides, harvest coverage, tasting routes, and a practical wineries list.',
  mainEntity: {
    '@type': 'Organization',
    name: 'Bellie Acres Wine',
    url: 'https://bellieacreswine.com/',
    email: 'executerceo@gmail.com',
    description:
      'Independent editorial guide to Temecula Valley wine country for trip planning — long-form guides, maps, and estate context.',
  },
};
---

<Layout
  title="About Bellie Acres Wine — Temecula Wine Country Guides"
  description="About Bellie Acres Wine: who publishes this Temecula wine guide, our editorial approach, harvest and tasting coverage, and how we help visitors plan wine country trips."
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <Navbar />

  <main class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 py-16">
    <p class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[2px] text-[var(--accent)] font-medium mb-3">Publisher</p>
    <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl md:text-6xl font-serif tracking-tight mb-6 text-stone-900">
      About Bellie Acres Wine
    </h1>
    <p class="text-xl text-stone-600 leading-relaxed mb-10">
      Bellie Acres Wine is an independent <strong>Temecula Valley wine-country publisher</strong> at
      <strong>bellieacreswine.com</strong>. We write practical guides for visitors — harvest season, tasting routes,
      weekday vs weekend pacing, views, pets, pairings — and we maintain a clear list and map so those articles connect
      to real estates you can visit.
    </p>

    <article class="space-y-6 text-lg text-stone-700 leading-relaxed">
      <p>
        Years ago, many small publishers could drop AdSense on a thin page and move on. Today Google’s review bots expect
        something closer to a <em>content site with a point of view</em>: who you are, what you cover, and enough original
        writing that an ad system can understand the page. That is the standard we build toward — not a bare link farm,
        and not a single-winery brochure.
      </p>

      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl text-stone-900 pt-4">Who publishes this site</h2>
      <p>
        Bellie Acres Wine is operated as a local Southern California project focused on Temecula Valley travel and wine
        education for adults. Editorial and site operations are handled under the Bellie Acres Wine name; business and
        correction emails go to
        <a class="text-[var(--accent)] underline" href="mailto:executerceo@gmail.com">executerceo@gmail.com</a>. We are
        based in the Temecula / Southern California area and write for people actually planning a day or weekend among
        the hills — not for generic “wine affiliate” spam.
      </p>
      <p>
        Related local real-estate context (moving to Temecula, estate questions) is handled separately via
        <a class="text-[var(--accent)] underline" href="https://lauradfarley.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"
          >lauradfarley.com</a
        >
        when relevant. The wine site itself does not sell homes or alcohol.
      </p>

      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl text-stone-900 pt-4">What we publish</h2>
      <p>Our core inventory is long-form and mid-form articles, including:</p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
        <li>
          <a class="text-[var(--accent)] underline" href="/guides/temecula-harvest-season">Harvest season in Temecula Valley</a>
          — timing, varietals, destination and boutique estates, visitor tips
        </li>
        <li>
          <a class="text-[var(--accent)] underline" href="/guides/best-temecula-wineries">Best Temecula wineries</a> — how
          we think about “best,” not a single universal ranking
        </li>
        <li>
          <a class="text-[var(--accent)] underline" href="/guides/first-timer-tasting-route">First-timer tasting routes</a>,
          <a class="text-[var(--accent)] underline" href="/guides/weekend-in-temecula-wine-country">weekend pacing</a>, and
          <a class="text-[var(--accent)] underline" href="/guides/weekday-vs-weekend-tasting">weekday vs weekend</a>
        </li>
        <li>
          Style and place guides:
          <a class="text-[var(--accent)] underline" href="/guides/temecula-red-varietals">red varietals</a>,
          <a class="text-[var(--accent)] underline" href="/guides/sip-with-a-view">sip with a view</a>,
          <a class="text-[var(--accent)] underline" href="/guides/pet-friendly-wineries">pet-friendly estates</a>,
          <a class="text-[var(--accent)] underline" href="/pairings">pairings</a>
        </li>
        <li>
          Free planning tools such as the
          <a class="text-[var(--accent)] underline" href="/wine-day-planner/">Wine Day Planner PDF</a>
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Alongside the guides, we keep a structured <a class="text-[var(--accent)] underline" href="/wineries">wineries list</a>
        and <a class="text-[var(--accent)] underline" href="/map">wine map</a> so readers can move from an article to a
        concrete stop. Estate pages add context (varietals, vibe, practical notes). Those pages support the journalism;
        they are not the only thing on the site.
      </p>

      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl text-stone-900 pt-4">Editorial standards</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
        <li>We write for trip planning: pacing, corridors, heat, reservations, and responsible tasting.</li>
        <li>We label independence clearly — we are not the official site of any winery unless a page says otherwise.</li>
        <li>We do not sell alcohol on this website and we do not take tasting reservations.</li>
        <li>Hours, fees, pet rules, and events change. We urge readers to confirm on the estate’s official site before driving.</li>
        <li>Featured listings, when present, are paid placements for discovery. Editorial guides are written to stay useful either way.</li>
        <li>Alcohol content is framed for adults 21+ with a sitewide responsibility notice.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl text-stone-900 pt-4">Why Temecula</h2>
      <p>
        Temecula Valley is one of Southern California’s most accessible wine destinations — dozens of tasting rooms in
        the rolling hills of Riverside County, roughly an hour from many coastal and inland cities depending on traffic.
        Elevation, marine influence, and varied soils support crisp whites, sparkling programs, bold reds, and
        Mediterranean-leaning blends. Harvest often runs from late summer into fall, with early whites and sparkling fruit
        ahead of the bigger reds — which is why seasonal coverage matters as much as a static list.
      </p>
      <p>
        Visitors still waste time on contradictory blog posts and outdated hours. Our job is to reduce that friction with
        clear structure, honest limits, and guides you can finish in one sitting before you leave the hotel.
      </p>

      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl text-stone-900 pt-4">How to use the site</h2>
      <ol class="list-decimal pl-6 space-y-2">
        <li>Start with a guide that matches your trip (harvest, first-timer, weekend, pets, views).</li>
        <li>Open the map or list to cluster stops on one corridor.</li>
        <li>Read two or three estate pages, then book or call the properties directly.</li>
        <li>Optional: download the free Wine Day Planner PDF for Day 1 / Day 2 templates.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl text-stone-900 pt-4">Advertising & privacy</h2>
      <p>
        We may display ads (including Google AdSense) and offer winery featured listings. Ads help keep guides free to
        read. Our
        <a class="text-[var(--accent)] underline" href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> explains cookies, AdSense, and
        contact data.
        <a class="text-[var(--accent)] underline" href="/terms">Terms of Use</a> cover acceptable use. Wineries interested
        in placement can see <a class="text-[var(--accent)] underline" href="/advertise">Advertise</a>.
      </p>

      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl text-stone-900 pt-4">Corrections</h2>
      <p>
        Own a Temecula estate or spot something outdated? Email
        <a class="text-[var(--accent)] underline" href="mailto:executerceo@gmail.com">executerceo@gmail.com</a>
        or use the <a class="text-[var(--accent)] underline" href="/contact">contact page</a>. We prefer accurate local
        information over a pretty mistake.
      </p>

      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl text-stone-900 pt-4">Visit responsibly</h2>
      <p>
        Alcohol service is for adults 21+. Designate a driver, use rideshare, or book a shuttle if you plan multiple
        tastings. Harvest and festival days get busy — leave margin for parking, heat, and a real meal between pours.
      </p>

      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl text-stone-900 pt-4">A note on seasons</h2>
      <p>
        Temecula is not a one-weekend story. Spring brings milder patio weather; summer heat pushes many visitors toward
        earlier seatings and indoor pours; late summer into fall is harvest energy — crush, stomps, and Wine Month style
        calendars. Winter can be quiet and beautiful for people who want fewer crowds. Our guides are written to match
        those rhythms so you are not using a July plan in October.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you are a returning reader, start at
        <a class="text-[var(--accent)] underline" href="/guides">Guides</a>. If you already know the valley, use the list
        as a fast filter and still skim one seasonal article so your plan matches the week you are actually visiting.
      </p>
      <p>
        Thank you for reading Bellie Acres Wine. We will keep the guides practical, the tone adult, and the planning tools
        secondary to the writing.
      </p>
    </article>

    <div class="mt-14 grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
      <a href="/guides/temecula-harvest-season" class="rounded-3xl border border-stone-200 bg-white p-6 hover:shadow-md transition">
        <div class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[2px] text-[var(--accent)] font-medium">Read next</div>
        <div class="font-serif text-2xl mt-1">Harvest season guide →</div>
      </a>
      <a href="/guides" class="rounded-3xl border border-stone-200 bg-white p-6 hover:shadow-md transition">
        <div class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[2px] text-[var(--accent)] font-medium">Library</div>
        <div class="font-serif text-2xl mt-1">All Temecula guides →</div>
      </a>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-10">
      <RelocateCta variant="card" />
    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>
